Work directly in the existing hiyroscript/alva repository on the current main codebase.

Implement the second playable fighter, #0002, and add a fighter-palette explosion effect when any fighter is absorbed by the Void.

Before changing anything, inspect the existing code and preserve Alva’s current architecture, coding conventions, comments, accessibility, responsive behavior, localization, game feel, and tests. Do not redesign unrelated systems.

Goals

1. Add #0002 as the second selectable/playable fighter.
2. #0002 currently only has finished idle and walking artwork. Do not invent attacks, attack animations, defense animations, jump animations, hurt animations, transformations, special moves, or other combat art.
3. Add the supplied sprite-source credit for #0002.
4. Never display or introduce the source artwork’s character/title name anywhere in the project. The fighter must only be referred to as #0002.
5. When a fighter is absorbed by the Void, create a short explosion/burst exactly where that fighter disappears.
6. The explosion must use a color palette derived from/matched to that fighter rather than one generic color shared by every fighter.
7. Preserve all existing Void scoring, respawn, double-KO, camera, combat, physics, and timing rules.

Existing architecture to preserve

The relevant code currently works like this:

* js/data/characters.js
    * CHARACTERS is the fighter database.
    * The file is intentionally structured so new fighters are data-driven.
    * The roster and battle systems should not need fighter-specific branches.
    * characterFramePaths(def) gathers animation/projectile/effect assets for loading.
* js/ui/fighter-roster.js
    * Builds the 48-slot roster directly from CHARACTERS.
    * Available characters automatically get selectable buttons, portraits, previews, and loading.
    * The preview uses the fighter’s idle animation.
    * Do not build a separate #0002 roster implementation.
* js/core/app.js
    * Preloads every available fighter.
    * loadCharacter() and SpriteSet.build() should continue to be the shared loading path.
* js/game/arena.js
    * checkVoid(fighters) finds fighters whose centers crossed the fixed Void boundary.
    * Fighters become lostToVoid, then onVoid(f) is called.
    * A lostToVoid fighter is immediately removed from inPlay, so it is no longer updated, targeted, collided with, or rendered.
    * This is the shared hook used by Quick Battle, Watch Mode, and Practice.
* js/game/battle.js
    * Battle.onVoid() handles points, match-winning falls, and respawn.
    * Do not move visual-effect logic into scoring logic.
* js/game/hit-fx.js
    * Owns presentation-only combat effects such as flashes, sparks, trails, shake, lethal zoom, and rebound effects.
    * It must remain presentation-only.
    * The new Void explosion belongs here or in a similarly presentation-only module, not in physics/combat data.
* js/game/arena.js rendering order currently paints fighters/effects, foreground, then the actual Void layer.
    * A Void explosion needs to remain visible even after the fighter has been swallowed.
    * Draw the new Void explosion after theme.drawVoid(...), but before UI/status/debug overlays as appropriate.

